Input: {"question": "When was Thomas Belasyse born?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d00", "start": 0, "end": 80, "text": "Thomas Belasyse, 1st Earl Fauconberg Thomas Belasyse, 1st Earl Fauconberg PC (c."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d00", "start": 81, "end": 126, "text": "1627 – 31 December 1700) was an English peer."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d00", "start": 127, "end": 269, "text": "He supported the Parliamentary cause in the English Civil War, becoming close to Oliver Cromwell and marrying Cromwell's third daughter, Mary."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d00", "start": 270, "end": 408, "text": "After the Restoration of the monarchy he became a member of the Privy Council to Charles II and was elevated to an earldom by William III."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d00", "start": 409, "end": 442, "text": "Belasyse was the only son of Hon."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d00", "start": 443, "end": 526, "text": "Henry Belasyse, who was the eldest son of Thomas Belasyse, 1st Viscount Fauconberg."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d00", "start": 527, "end": 615, "text": "Unlike his Royalist father and grandfather, Belasyse supported Parliament in the English"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d01", "start": 0, "end": 64, "text": "father Grace Belasyse mother Sir Rowland Belasyse, of Smithel..."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d01", "start": 65, "end": 324, "text": "brother Grace Saunderson sister Arabella Frankland sister Barbara Belasyse sister Frances Jones sister About Thomas Belasyse, 2nd Viscount & 1st Earl Fauconberg, PC Thomas Belasyse, 1st Earl of Fauconberg was baptised on 16 March 1590.2 He was the son of Hon."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d01", "start": 325, "end": 584, "text": "Henry Belasyse and Grace Barton.2,3 He married, firstly, Mildred Saunderson, daughter of Nicholas Saunderson, 2nd Viscount Castleton and Frances Manners, on 3 July 1651.3 He married, secondly, Mary Cromwell, daughter of Oliver Cromwell and Elizabeth Bouchier."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d02", "start": 0, "end": 145, "text": "Thomas Belasyse, 1st Earl Fauconberg (second creation) Thomas Belasyse, 1st Earl Fauconberg (27 April 1699 – 8 February 1774) was a British peer."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d02", "start": 146, "end": 290, "text": "Fauconberg was the son and heir of Thomas Belasyse, 3rd Viscount Fauconberg, by his wife Bridget Gage, a daughter of Sir John Gage, 4th Baronet."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d02", "start": 291, "end": 407, "text": "He was raised as a Roman Catholic, but made a public abjuration of the faith and converted to the Church of England."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d02", "start": 408, "end": 476, "text": "Fauconberg succeeded to his father's viscountcy on 26 November 1718."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d02", "start": 477, "end": 572, "text": "He served as a Lord of the Bedchamber to George II between 1738 and 1760, and was made a member"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d03", "start": 0, "end": 520, "text": "+ Birth date string 27 April 1699 + Birth day 27 + Birth month 4 + Birth year 1,699 + Children-list1 Henry Belasyse , 2nd Earl Fauconberg ( 1743-1802 ) +Anne Belasyse ( bef1746-1768 ) + Death blurb 8 February 1774 + Death date February 8 , 1774 + Death date string 8 February 1774 + Death day 8 + Death month 2 + Death year 1,774 + Familysearch afn 9FN7-LB + Father Thomas Belasyse , 3rd Viscount Fauconberg ( -1718 ) + Given name Thomas + Ifmarried-g1 true + Joined with Catherine Betham ( c1719-1760 ) + Joined with-g1"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d04", "start": 0, "end": 541, "text": "tree descendants Thomas Belasyse , 1st Earl Fauconberg ‡ Birth : 27 April 1699 Death : 8 February 1774 Remains : May 1774 Coxwold , Yorkshire , England , United Kingdom Father : Thomas Belasyse , 3rd Viscount Fauconberg ( -1718 ) Mother : Bridget Gage ( -1732 ) Titles : 1st Earl Fauconberg Spouse / partner : Catherine Betham ( c1719-1760 ) Wedding : 5 August 1726 Sex : Familysearch afn : 9FN7-LB Edit Facts Biography Thomas Belasyse , 1st Earl Fauconberg , was born 27 April 1699 to Thomas Belasyse , 3rd Viscount Fauconberg ( -1718 ) and"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d05", "start": 0, "end": 18, "text": "as Baron Belasyse."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d05", "start": 19, "end": 366, "text": "Thomas Belasyse, 1st Viscount Fauconberg Thomas Belasyse, 1st Viscount Fauconberg (1577 – 18 April 1653), styled Baron Fauconberg between 1627 and 1643 and Sir Thomas Belasyse, 2nd Baronet between 1624 and 1627, was an English politician who sat in the House of Commons at various times between 1597 and 1624 and was raised to the peerage in 1627."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d05", "start": 367, "end": 441, "text": "He was an ardent supporter of the Royalist cause in the English Civil War."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d05", "start": 442, "end": 594, "text": "Before the Civil War, Belasyse and his family had a long running confrontation with William Wentworth, a close advisor to King Charles I, primarily over"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d06", "start": 0, "end": 28, "text": "Thirsk , 27 September 1604 ."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d06", "start": 29, "end": 127, "text": "His wife is said to have died in 1571 , but she is named in his mother 's will , written in 1577 ."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d06", "start": 128, "end": 171, "text": "Sir Henry Belasyse ( 1555-1624 ) , 1st bt ."}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d06", "start": 172, "end": 213, "text": "Belasyse , Sir Henry ( 1555-1624 ) , kt ."}, "D7S5": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d06", "start": 214, "end": 226, "text": "and 1st bt ."}, "D7S6": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d06", "start": 227, "end": 304, "text": "Third but eldest surviving son of Sir William Belasyse ( c.1523-1604 ) , kt ."}, "D7S7": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d06", "start": 305, "end": 435, "text": "and his wife Margaret , daughter of Sir Nicholas Fairfax of Walton and Gilling ( Yorks NR ) , baptised at Coxwold , 14 June 1555 ."}, "D7S8": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d06", "start": 436, "end": 461, "text": "Educated at Jesus College"}, "D8S1": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0369-a4f70f2943f4:d07", "start": 0, "end": 731, "text": "at Jesus College 0 references conflict English Civil War 0 references member of 4th Parliament of King James I 0 references Addled Parliament 0 references Identifiers VIAF cluster ID 62967540 1 reference imported from Wikimedia project English Wikipedia FAST ID 154533 0 references Library of Congress authority ID n85029983 0 references WorldCat Entities ID E39PBJyCFDqRFvCrRHrgYJjHmd 1 reference matched by identifier from Library of Congress Authorities Library of Congress authority ID n85029983 retrieved 11 April 2024 Beamish peerage database person ID 3731 0 references Cambridge Alumni Database ID BLSS592T 0 references Freebase ID /m/0bh81w_ 0 references History of Parliament ID 1